# Nyx Task Queue

Describe work to the Dispatch prompt and it appends tasks here. The dispatcher
reads tasks under `## Active Tasks` and runs them on the 96-slot grid. Keep the
section empty until you queue something.

## Active Tasks

## Completed

---

## Task format (reference — only lines under `## Active Tasks` are parsed)

```
- [ ] TASK-ID — Short description
      [type: code|content|analysis|assistant|pipeline]
      [model: sonnet|opus|haiku]
      [gate: typecheck,tests|none]
      [slot: N]            daily at slot N (0–95)
      [every: 3h]          cadence anchored at slot 0
      [repo: org/name]     for code/analysis/pipeline against an external repo
```

A task has at most one of `[slot:]` or `[every:]`; with neither it joins the
standing list. See `CLAUDE.md` (Dispatch mode) for the full tag reference.
